#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SQD for energy estimation of a chemistry Hamiltonian {#sqd-for-energy-"
"estimation-of-a-chemistry-hamiltonian}"
msgstr ""
"SQD untuk estimasi energi dari Hamiltonian kimia {#sqd-for-energy-"
"estimation-of-a-chemistry-hamiltonian}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson, we will apply SQD to estimate the ground state energy of a "
"molecule.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di pelajaran ini, kita akan menerapkan SQD untuk mengestimasi energi ground "
"state dari sebuah molekul.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In particular, we will discuss the following topics using the $4$-step "
"Qiskit pattern approach:\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara khusus, kita akan membahas topik-topik berikut menggunakan pendekatan"
" pola Qiskit $4$-langkah:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map problem to quantum circuits and operators\n"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Peta masalah ke circuit dan operator kuantum\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Setup the molecular Hamiltonian for $N_2$.\n"
msgstr "Siapkan Hamiltonian molekuler untuk $N_2$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Explain the chemistry-inspired and hardware-friendly local unitary cluster "
"Jastrow (LUCJ) [\\[1\\]](#references)\n"
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan local unitary cluster Jastrow (LUCJ) yang terinspirasi dari kimia "
"dan ramah hardware [\\[1\\]](#references)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize for target hardware\n"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimalkan untuk hardware target\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Optimize gate counts and layout of the ansatz for hardware execution\n"
msgstr "Optimalkan jumlah Gate dan tata letak ansatz untuk eksekusi hardware\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute on target hardware\n"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Eksekusi pada hardware target\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run the optimized circuit on a real QPU to generate samples of the "
"subspace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jalankan Circuit yang telah dioptimalkan pada QPU nyata untuk menghasilkan "
"sampel dari subspace.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process results\n"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses hasil\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Introduce the self-consistent configuration recovery loop "
"[\\[2\\]](#references)\n"
msgstr ""
"Perkenalkan loop pemulihan konfigurasi self-consistent "
"[\\[2\\]](#references)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '        - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Post-process the full set of bitstring samples, using prior knowledge of "
"particle number and the average orbital occupancy calculated on the most "
"recent iteration.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pasca-proses seluruh set sampel bitstring, menggunakan pengetahuan "
"sebelumnya tentang jumlah partikel dan rata-rata hunian orbital yang "
"dihitung pada iterasi terakhir.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '        - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Probabilistically create batches of subsamples from recovered bitstrings.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara probabilistik buat batch subsampel dari bitstring yang dipulihkan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '        - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Project and diagonalize the molecular Hamiltonian over each sampled "
"subspace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Proyeksikan dan diagonalisasi Hamiltonian molekuler pada setiap subspace "
"yang diambil.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '        - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Save the minimum ground state energy found across all batches and update the"
" avg orbital occupancy.\n"
msgstr ""
"Simpan energi ground state minimum yang ditemukan di semua batch dan "
"perbarui rata-rata hunian orbital.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will use several software packages throughout the lesson.\n"
"- `PySCF` to define the molecule and setup the Hamiltonian.\n"
"- `ffsim` package to construct the LUCJ ansatz.\n"
"- `Qiskit` for transpiling the ansatz for hardware execution.\n"
"- `Qiskit IBM Runtime` to execute the circuit on a QPU and collect samples.\n"
"- `Qiskit addon SQD` configuration recovery and ground state energy estimation using subspace projection and matrix diagonalization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan menggunakan beberapa paket perangkat lunak sepanjang pelajaran.\n"
"- `PySCF` untuk mendefinisikan molekul dan menyiapkan Hamiltonian.\n"
"- paket `ffsim` untuk membangun ansatz LUCJ.\n"
"- `Qiskit` untuk mentranspile ansatz untuk eksekusi hardware.\n"
"- `Qiskit IBM Runtime` untuk mengeksekusi Circuit pada QPU dan mengumpulkan sampel.\n"
"- `Qiskit addon SQD` untuk pemulihan konfigurasi dan estimasi energi ground state menggunakan proyeksi subspace dan diagonalisasi matriks.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1. Map problem to quantum circuits and operators {#1-map-problem-to-quantum-"
"circuits-and-operators}"
msgstr ""
"1. Peta masalah ke circuit dan operator kuantum {#1-map-problem-to-quantum-"
"circuits-and-operators}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Molecular Hamiltonian {#molecular-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Hamiltonian molekuler {#molecular-hamiltonian}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "A molecular Hamiltonian takes the generic form:\n"
msgstr "Sebuah Hamiltonian molekuler memiliki bentuk umum:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum_{ \\substack{pr\\\\\\sigma} } h_{pr} \\, \\hat{a}^\\dagger_{p\\sigma} \\hat{a}_{r\\sigma}\n"
"+\n"
"\\sum_{ \\substack{prqs\\\\\\sigma\\tau} }\n"
"\\frac{(pr|qs)}{2} \\,\n"
"\\hat{a}^\\dagger_{p\\sigma}\n"
"\\hat{a}^\\dagger_{q\\tau}\n"
"\\hat{a}_{s\\tau}\n"
"\\hat{a}_{r\\sigma}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum_{ \\substack{pr\\\\\\sigma} } h_{pr} \\, \\hat{a}^\\dagger_{p\\sigma} \\hat{a}_{r\\sigma}\n"
"+\n"
"\\sum_{ \\substack{prqs\\\\\\sigma\\tau} }\n"
"\\frac{(pr|qs)}{2} \\,\n"
"\\hat{a}^\\dagger_{p\\sigma}\n"
"\\hat{a}^\\dagger_{q\\tau}\n"
"\\hat{a}_{s\\tau}\n"
"\\hat{a}_{r\\sigma}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\\hat{a}^\\dagger_{p\\sigma}$/$\\hat{a}_{p\\sigma}$ are the fermionic "
"creation/annihilation operators associated to the $p$-th basis set element "
"and the spin $\\sigma$. $h_{pr}$ and $(pr|qs)$ are the one- and two-body "
"electronic integrals. Using pySCF, we will define the molecule and compute "
"the one- and two-body integrals of the Hamiltonian for basis set `6-31g`.\n"
msgstr ""
"$\\hat{a}^\\dagger_{p\\sigma}$/$\\hat{a}_{p\\sigma}$ adalah operator "
"penciptaan/pemusnahan fermionik yang terkait dengan elemen basis set ke-$p$ "
"dan spin $\\sigma$. $h_{pr}$ dan $(pr|qs)$ adalah integral elektronik satu- "
"dan dua-badan. Menggunakan pySCF, kita akan mendefinisikan molekul dan "
"menghitung integral satu- dan dua-badan dari Hamiltonian untuk basis set "
"`6-31g`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson, we will use Jordan-Wigner (JW) transformation to map a "
"fermionic wavefunction to a qubit wavefunction so that it can be prepared "
"using a quantum circuit. The JW transformation maps the Fock space of "
"fermions in M spatial orbitals onto the Hilbert space of 2M qubits, that is,"
" a spatial orbital is split into two _spin orbitals_, one associated with a "
"spin up ($\\alpha$) electron and another with spin down ($\\beta$). A spin "
"orbital can be occupied or unoccupied. Usually, when we refer to number of "
"orbitals, we will be using number of _spatial_ orbitals. The number of spin "
"orbitals will be double. In quantum circuits, we will represent each spin "
"orbital with one qubit. Thus, a set of qubits will represent spin-up or "
"$\\alpha$-orbitals, and another set will represent spin-down or "
"$\\beta$-orbitals. For example, $N_2$ molecule for `6-31g` basis set has "
"$16$ spatial orbitals (that is, $16$ $\\alpha$ + $16$ $\\beta$ = $32$ spin "
"orbitals). Thus, we will need a $32$-qubit quantum circuit (we may need "
"extra ancilla qubits as discussed later). The qubits are measured in "
"computational basis to generate bitstrings, which represent electronic "
"configurations or (Slater) determinants. Throughout this lesson, we will use"
" the terms bitstrings, configurations, and determinants interchangeably. The"
" bitstrings tell us electron occupancy in spin orbitals: a $1$ in a bit "
"position means the corresponding spin orbital is occupied, while a $0$ means"
" the spin orbital is empty. As electronic structure problems are particle "
"preserving, only a fixed number of spin orbitals must be occupied. The $N_2$"
" molecule has $5$ spin-up ($\\alpha$) and $5$ spin-down ($\\beta$) "
"electrons. Thus, any bitstring representing the $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ "
"orbitals must have five $1\\text{s}$ each for $N_2$ molecule.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di pelajaran ini, kita akan menggunakan transformasi Jordan-Wigner (JW) "
"untuk memetakan fungsi gelombang fermionik ke fungsi gelombang qubit agar "
"bisa disiapkan menggunakan Circuit kuantum. Transformasi JW memetakan ruang "
"Fock fermion dalam M orbital spasial ke ruang Hilbert dari 2M qubit, yaitu, "
"sebuah orbital spasial dibagi menjadi dua _orbital spin_, satu terkait "
"dengan elektron spin naik ($\\alpha$) dan satu lagi dengan spin turun "
"($\\beta$). Sebuah orbital spin bisa terisi atau kosong. Biasanya, saat kita"
" menyebut jumlah orbital, kita menggunakan jumlah orbital _spasial_. Jumlah "
"orbital spin akan dua kali lipatnya. Dalam Circuit kuantum, kita akan "
"merepresentasikan setiap orbital spin dengan satu qubit. Jadi, satu set "
"qubit akan merepresentasikan orbital spin-naik atau $\\alpha$-orbital, dan "
"set lainnya akan merepresentasikan orbital spin-turun atau $\\beta$-orbital."
" Misalnya, molekul $N_2$ untuk basis set `6-31g` memiliki $16$ orbital "
"spasial (yaitu, $16$ $\\alpha$ + $16$ $\\beta$ = $32$ orbital spin). Dengan "
"demikian, kita membutuhkan Circuit kuantum $32$-qubit (kita mungkin "
"memerlukan qubit ancilla tambahan seperti yang dibahas nanti). Qubit diukur "
"dalam basis komputasi untuk menghasilkan bitstring, yang merepresentasikan "
"konfigurasi elektronik atau determinan (Slater). Sepanjang pelajaran ini, "
"kita akan menggunakan istilah bitstring, konfigurasi, dan determinan secara "
"bergantian. Bitstring memberi tahu kita hunian elektron dalam orbital spin: "
"nilai $1$ di posisi bit berarti orbital spin yang sesuai terisi, sedangkan "
"$0$ berarti orbital spin kosong. Karena masalah struktur elektronik bersifat"
" konservasi partikel, hanya sejumlah tetap orbital spin yang harus terisi. "
"Molekul $N_2$ memiliki $5$ elektron spin-naik ($\\alpha$) dan $5$ spin-turun"
" ($\\beta$). Jadi, setiap bitstring yang merepresentasikan orbital $\\alpha$"
" dan $\\beta$ harus memiliki lima $1$ masing-masing untuk molekul $N_2$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1.1 Quantum circuit for sample generation: The LUCJ ansatz {#11-quantum-"
"circuit-for-sample-generation-the-lucj-ansatz}"
msgstr ""
"1.1 Circuit kuantum untuk pembuatan sampel: Ansatz LUCJ {#11-quantum-"
"circuit-for-sample-generation-the-lucj-ansatz}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson, we will use the local unitary coupled cluster Jastrow (LUCJ)"
" [\\\\[1\\\\]](#references) ansatz for quantum state preparation and "
"subsequent sampling. First, we will explain different building blocks of the"
" full UCJ ansatz and the approximations made in the local version of it. "
"Next, by using ffsim package, we will construct the LUCJ ansatz and optimize"
" it using Qiskit transpiler for hardware execution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di pelajaran ini, kita akan menggunakan ansatz local unitary coupled cluster"
" Jastrow (LUCJ) [\\\\[1\\\\]](#references) untuk persiapan keadaan kuantum "
"dan pengambilan sampel berikutnya. Pertama, kita akan menjelaskan berbagai "
"blok bangunan dari ansatz UCJ penuh dan aproksimasi yang dibuat dalam versi "
"lokalnya. Selanjutnya, dengan menggunakan paket ffsim, kita akan membangun "
"ansatz LUCJ dan mengoptimalkannya menggunakan Transpiler Qiskit untuk "
"eksekusi hardware.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The UCJ ansatz has the following form (for a product of $L$ layers or "
"repetitions of the UCJ operator.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Ansatz UCJ memiliki bentuk berikut (untuk hasil kali $L$ lapisan atau "
"pengulangan operator UCJ.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\prod_{\\mu=1}^{L}{(e^{K^{\\mu}} \\times {e^{iJ^{\\mu}}} \\times {e^{-K^{\\mu}}})} |\\Phi_{0}\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\prod_{\\mu=1}^{L}{(e^{K^{\\mu}} \\times {e^{iJ^{\\mu}}} \\times {e^{-K^{\\mu}}})} |\\Phi_{0}\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where, $\\vert \\Phi_{0} \\rangle$ is a reference state, typically taken as the Hartree-Fock (HF) state. As the Hartree-Fock state is defined as having the lowest numbered orbitals occupied, the HF state preparation will involve applying X gates to set qubits corresponding to occupied orbitals to one. For example, the HF state preparation block for 4 spatial orbitals and 2 up- and 2 down-spin may look like the following:\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing 8 qubits, 4 called alpha orbitals and 4 called beta orbitals. The top two alpha and the top two beta have a \"not\" gate.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig1.svg)\n"
"A single repetition of the UCJ operator ${(e^{K^{(\\mu)}} \\times {e^{iJ^{(\\mu)}}} \\times {e^{-K^{(\\mu)}}})}$ consists of a diagonal Coulomb evolution ($e^{iJ^{(\\mu)}}$) sandwiched by orbital rotations ($e^{K^{(\\mu)}}$ and $e^{-K^{(\\mu)}}$).\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing that the UCJ circuit can be broken down into rotation layers and a diagonal Coulomb evolution layer.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig2.svg)\n"
"Orbital rotation blocks work on a single spin species ($\\alpha$ (up-spin)/$\\beta$ (down-spin)). For each electron species, orbital rotation consists of a layer of single-qubit $R_{z}$ gates followed by a sequence of 2-qubit Given's rotation gates ($XX + YY$ gates).\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana, $\\vert \\Phi_{0} \\rangle$ adalah keadaan referensi, biasanya diambil sebagai keadaan Hartree-Fock (HF). Karena keadaan Hartree-Fock didefinisikan memiliki orbital bernomor terendah yang terisi, persiapan keadaan HF akan melibatkan penerapan Gate X untuk mengatur qubit yang sesuai dengan orbital yang terisi menjadi satu. Misalnya, blok persiapan keadaan HF untuk 4 orbital spasial dan 2 spin-naik dan 2 spin-turun mungkin terlihat seperti berikut:\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing 8 qubits, 4 called alpha orbitals and 4 called beta orbitals. The top two alpha and the top two beta have a \"not\" gate.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig1.svg)\n"
"Satu pengulangan dari operator UCJ ${(e^{K^{(\\mu)}} \\times {e^{iJ^{(\\mu)}}} \\times {e^{-K^{(\\mu)}}})}$ terdiri dari evolusi Coulomb diagonal ($e^{iJ^{(\\mu)}}$) yang diapit oleh rotasi orbital ($e^{K^{(\\mu)}}$ dan $e^{-K^{(\\mu)}}$).\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing that the UCJ circuit can be broken down into rotation layers and a diagonal Coulomb evolution layer.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig2.svg)\n"
"Blok rotasi orbital bekerja pada satu spesies spin ($\\alpha$ (spin-naik)/$\\beta$ (spin-turun)). Untuk setiap spesies elektron, rotasi orbital terdiri dari lapisan Gate $R_{z}$ satu-qubit diikuti oleh urutan Gate rotasi Given's dua-qubit ($XX + YY$ gates).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The 2-qubit gates act on adjacent spin-orbitals (nearest neighbor qubits), and therefore, are implementable on IBM&reg; QPUs without the need for SWAP gates.\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing 4 alpha orbital qubits and 4 beta orbital qubits. The circuits start with R-Z gates, and then have a series of Given's rotation gates.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig3.svg)\n"
"The $e^{iJ^{(\\mu)}}$, also known as the diagonal Coulomb operator, consists of three blocks. Two of them work on same spin sectors ($e^{iJ_{\\alpha \\alpha}^{(\\mu)}}$ and $e^{iJ_{\\beta \\beta}^{(\\mu)}}$), and one works between two spin sectors ($e^{iJ_{\\alpha \\beta}^{(\\mu)}}$).\n"
msgstr ""
"Gate dua-qubit bekerja pada orbital-spin yang berdekatan (qubit tetangga terdekat), dan oleh karena itu, dapat diimplementasikan pada QPU IBM&reg; tanpa memerlukan Gate SWAP.\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing 4 alpha orbital qubits and 4 beta orbital qubits. The circuits start with R-Z gates, and then have a series of Given's rotation gates.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig3.svg)\n"
"$e^{iJ^{(\\mu)}}$, yang juga dikenal sebagai operator Coulomb diagonal, terdiri dari tiga blok. Dua di antaranya bekerja pada sektor spin yang sama ($e^{iJ_{\\alpha \\alpha}^{(\\mu)}}$ dan $e^{iJ_{\\beta \\beta}^{(\\mu)}}$), dan satu bekerja antara dua sektor spin ($e^{iJ_{\\alpha \\beta}^{(\\mu)}}$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All the blocks in $e^{iJ^{(\\mu)}}$ consists of number-number gates "
"$U_{nn}(\\phi)$ [\\[1\\]](#references). A $U_{nn}(\\phi)$ gate can be "
"further broken down into a $R_{ZZ}(\\frac{\\phi}{2})$ gate followed by two "
"single-qubit $Rz(-\\frac{\\phi}{2})$ gates acting on two separate qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Semua blok dalam $e^{iJ^{(\\mu)}}$ terdiri dari Gate number-number "
"$U_{nn}(\\phi)$ [\\[1\\]](#references). Sebuah Gate $U_{nn}(\\phi)$ bisa "
"dipecah lebih lanjut menjadi Gate $R_{ZZ}(\\frac{\\phi}{2})$ diikuti oleh "
"dua Gate $Rz(-\\frac{\\phi}{2})$ satu-qubit yang bekerja pada dua qubit "
"terpisah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Same-spin components ($J_{\\alpha \\alpha}$ and $J_{\\beta \\beta}$) have "
"$U_{nn}$ gates between all possible pairs of qubits. However, as "
"superconducting QPUs have restrictive connectivity, qubits must be swapped "
"to realize gates between non-adjacent qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Komponen spin-sama ($J_{\\alpha \\alpha}$ dan $J_{\\beta \\beta}$) memiliki "
"Gate $U_{nn}$ antara semua pasangan qubit yang memungkinkan. Namun, karena "
"QPU superkonduktor memiliki konektivitas yang terbatas, qubit harus ditukar "
"untuk mewujudkan Gate antara qubit yang tidak berdekatan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, consider the following $e^{iJ_{\\alpha \\alpha}^{(\\mu)}}$ (or $e^{iJ_{\\beta \\beta}^{(\\mu)}}$) block for $N = 4$ spatial orbitals. For a linear qubit connectivity, the last three gates are not directly implementable as they work between non-adjacent qubits (for example, Q0 and Q2 are not directly connected). Therefore, we need SWAP gates to make them adjacent (following figure shows an example with $3$ SWAP gates).\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing linearly-coupled qubits and corresponding alpha/beta circuits.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig4.svg)\n"
"Next, the $J_{\\alpha \\beta}$ implements gates between same indexed orbitals from different spin sectors (for example, between $0\\alpha$ and $0\\beta$). Similarly, if the qubits are not physically adjacent on a QPU, these gates will also require SWAPs.\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing 4 alpha qubits connected to the 4 beta qubits.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig5.svg)\n"
"From the above discussion, the UCJ ansatz faces some hurdles for HW execution as it needs SWAP gates due to non-adjacent qubit interactions. The local variant of the UCJ ansatz, LUCJ, addresses this challenge by removing some $U_{nn}$ from the diagonal Coulomb operator.\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalnya, pertimbangkan blok $e^{iJ_{\\alpha \\alpha}^{(\\mu)}}$ (atau $e^{iJ_{\\beta \\beta}^{(\\mu)}}$) berikut untuk $N = 4$ orbital spasial. Untuk konektivitas qubit linier, tiga Gate terakhir tidak dapat langsung diimplementasikan karena bekerja antara qubit yang tidak berdekatan (misalnya, Q0 dan Q2 tidak terhubung langsung). Oleh karena itu, kita memerlukan Gate SWAP untuk membuatnya berdekatan (gambar berikut menunjukkan contoh dengan $3$ Gate SWAP).\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing linearly-coupled qubits and corresponding alpha/beta circuits.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig4.svg)\n"
"Selanjutnya, $J_{\\alpha \\beta}$ mengimplementasikan Gate antara orbital berindeks sama dari sektor spin yang berbeda (misalnya, antara $0\\alpha$ dan $0\\beta$). Demikian pula, jika qubit tidak secara fisik berdekatan pada QPU, Gate-Gate ini juga akan memerlukan SWAP.\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing 4 alpha qubits connected to the 4 beta qubits.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig5.svg)\n"
"Dari diskusi di atas, ansatz UCJ menghadapi beberapa kendala untuk eksekusi HW karena memerlukan Gate SWAP akibat interaksi qubit yang tidak berdekatan. Varian lokal dari ansatz UCJ, LUCJ, mengatasi tantangan ini dengan menghapus beberapa $U_{nn}$ dari operator Coulomb diagonal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the same electron species blocks, $J_{\\alpha \\alpha}$ and $J_{\\beta \\beta}$), we only keep the $U_{nn}$ gates compatible with nearest-neighbor connectivity and remove gates between non-adjacent qubits in the LUCJ version. Following figure shows the LUCJ block after removal of non-adjacent gates.\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing 4 alpha qubits and 4 beta qubits each with R-Z gates, followed by two-qubit gates.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig6.svg)\n"
"Next, the LUCJ version of the $J_{\\alpha \\beta}$ block that works between different electron species can take different shape based on the device topology.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada blok spesies elektron yang sama, $J_{\\alpha \\alpha}$ dan $J_{\\beta \\beta}$), kita hanya menyimpan Gate $U_{nn}$ yang kompatibel dengan konektivitas tetangga-terdekat dan menghapus Gate antara qubit yang tidak berdekatan dalam versi LUCJ. Gambar berikut menunjukkan blok LUCJ setelah penghapusan Gate non-berdekatan.\n"
"![A circuit diagram showing 4 alpha qubits and 4 beta qubits each with R-Z gates, followed by two-qubit gates.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig6.svg)\n"
"Selanjutnya, versi LUCJ dari blok $J_{\\alpha \\beta}$ yang bekerja antara spesies elektron yang berbeda bisa mengambil bentuk yang berbeda berdasarkan topologi perangkat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, also, the LUCJ version gets rid of non-compatible gates. The figure "
"below shows variants of the $J_{\\alpha \\beta}$ block for different qubit "
"topology including grid, hexagonal, heavy-hex, and linear.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini juga, versi LUCJ menghilangkan Gate yang tidak kompatibel. Gambar di"
" bawah menunjukkan varian dari blok $J_{\\alpha \\beta}$ untuk berbagai "
"topologi qubit termasuk grid, heksagonal, heavy-hex, dan linier.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Square**: we can have $U_{nn}$ gates between all $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ "
"orbitals without any SWAPs, and therefore, do not need to remove any "
"$U_{nn}$ gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Square**: kita bisa memiliki Gate $U_{nn}$ antara semua orbital $\\alpha$ "
"dan $\\beta$ tanpa SWAP apapun, dan oleh karena itu, tidak perlu menghapus "
"Gate $U_{nn}$ apapun.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Heavy-hex**: The $\\alpha$-$\\beta$ interactions are kept between every "
"$4$-th indexed (such as the 0th, 4th, and 8th) spin orbitals and are "
"_ancilla_ mediated, that is, we need ancilla qubits between the linear "
"chains representing $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ orbitals. This arrangement needs "
"a limited number of SWAPs.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Heavy-hex**: Interaksi $\\alpha$-$\\beta$ dijaga antara setiap orbital "
"berindeks ke-$4$ (seperti orbital ke-0, ke-4, dan ke-8) dan dimediasi "
"_ancilla_, yaitu, kita memerlukan qubit ancilla antara rantai linier yang "
"merepresentasikan orbital $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$. Susunan ini membutuhkan "
"jumlah SWAP yang terbatas.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Hexagonal**: Every other orbital, such as 0th, 2nd, and 4th indexed "
"orbitals, becomes nearest neighbors when $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are laid out"
" in two adjacent linear chains.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Hexagonal**: Setiap orbital lainnya, seperti orbital berindeks ke-0, ke-2,"
" dan ke-4, menjadi tetangga terdekat ketika $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$ disusun "
"dalam dua rantai linier yang berdekatan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- **Linear**: Only one $\\alpha$ and one $\\beta$ orbital are connected, which means the $J_{\\alpha \\beta}$ block will have only one gate.\n"
"![Connectivity diagrams for different qubit layouts. They show qubits arranged on a square grid, a hexagonal lattice, a heavy-hex lattice (hexagonal lattice with one extra qubit along each side of the hexagon), and a linear chain.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig7.svg)\n"
"While removing gates from the UCJ ansatz to construct the LUCJ version makes it more HW compatible, the ansatz loses some expressivity. Therefore, more repetitions ($L$) of the modified UCJ operator may be needed when using the LUCJ ansatz.\n"
msgstr ""
"- **Linear**: Hanya satu orbital $\\alpha$ dan satu $\\beta$ yang terhubung, yang berarti blok $J_{\\alpha \\beta}$ hanya akan memiliki satu Gate.\n"
"![Connectivity diagrams for different qubit layouts. They show qubits arranged on a square grid, a hexagonal lattice, a heavy-hex lattice (hexagonal lattice with one extra qubit along each side of the hexagon), and a linear chain.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig7.svg)\n"
"Meski menghapus Gate dari ansatz UCJ untuk membangun versi LUCJ membuatnya lebih kompatibel dengan HW, ansatz kehilangan sebagian ekspresivitasnya. Oleh karena itu, lebih banyak pengulangan ($L$) dari operator UCJ yang dimodifikasi mungkin diperlukan saat menggunakan ansatz LUCJ.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1.2 LUCJ ansatz initialization {#12-lucj-ansatz-initialization}"
msgstr "1.2 Inisialisasi ansatz LUCJ {#12-lucj-ansatz-initialization}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The LUCJ is a parameterized ansatz, and we need to initialize the parameters"
" before hardware execution. One way to initialize ansatz is by using `t1` "
"and `t2` amplitudes from classical coupled cluster singles and doubles "
"(CCSD) method, where `t1` amplitudes are the coefficient of single "
"excitation operators and `t2` amplitudes are for double excitation "
"operators.\n"
msgstr ""
"LUCJ adalah ansatz yang diparameterisasi, dan kita perlu menginisialisasi "
"parameter sebelum eksekusi hardware. Salah satu cara untuk menginisialisasi "
"ansatz adalah dengan menggunakan amplitudo `t1` dan `t2` dari metode coupled"
" cluster singles and doubles (CCSD) klasik, di mana amplitudo `t1` adalah "
"koefisien dari operator eksitasi tunggal dan amplitudo `t2` untuk operator "
"eksitasi ganda.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that while initializing the LUCJ ansatz with `t1` and `t2` amplitudes "
"generate decent results, the ansatz parameters may need further "
"optimization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa meskipun menginisialisasi ansatz LUCJ dengan amplitudo `t1`"
" dan `t2` menghasilkan hasil yang cukup baik, parameter ansatz mungkin perlu"
" dioptimalkan lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1.3 Constructing the LUCJ ansatz using `ffsim` {#13-constructing-the-lucj-"
"ansatz-using-ffsim}"
msgstr ""
"1.3 Membangun ansatz LUCJ menggunakan `ffsim` {#13-constructing-the-lucj-"
"ansatz-using-ffsim}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will use the [ffsim](https://github.com/qiskit-community/ffsim/tree/main)"
" package to create and initialize the ansatz with `t1` and `t2` amplitudes "
"computed above. Since our molecule has a closed-shell Hartree-Fock state, we"
" will use the spin-balanced variant of the UCJ ansatz, "
"[UCJOpSpinBalanced](https://qiskit-"
"community.github.io/ffsim/api/ffsim.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced).\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan menggunakan paket [ffsim](https://github.com/qiskit-"
"community/ffsim/tree/main) untuk membuat dan menginisialisasi ansatz dengan "
"amplitudo `t1` dan `t2` yang dihitung di atas. Karena molekul kita memiliki "
"keadaan Hartree-Fock closed-shell, kita akan menggunakan varian spin-"
"balanced dari ansatz UCJ, [UCJOpSpinBalanced](https://qiskit-"
"community.github.io/ffsim/api/ffsim.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As IBM hardware has a heavy-hex topology, we will adopt the _zig-zag_ "
"pattern used in [\\[1\\]](#references) and explained above for qubit "
"interactions. In this pattern, orbitals (qubits) with the same spin are "
"connected with a line topology (red and blue circles). Due to the heavy-hex "
"topology, orbitals for different spins have connections between every 4th "
"orbital, that is, the 0th, 4th, 8th, and so on (purple circles).\n"
msgstr ""
"Karena hardware IBM memiliki topologi heavy-hex, kita akan mengadopsi pola "
"_zig-zag_ yang digunakan dalam [\\[1\\]](#references) dan dijelaskan di atas"
" untuk interaksi qubit. Dalam pola ini, orbital (qubit) dengan spin yang "
"sama terhubung dengan topologi garis (lingkaran merah dan biru). Karena "
"topologi heavy-hex, orbital untuk spin yang berbeda memiliki koneksi antara "
"setiap orbital ke-4, yaitu orbital ke-0, ke-4, ke-8, dan seterusnya "
"(lingkaran ungu).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A zig-zag pattern traced out along a heavy-hex "
"lattice.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-"
"algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig8.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A zig-zag pattern traced out along a heavy-hex "
"lattice.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-"
"algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig8.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The LUCJ ansatz with repeated layers can be optimized by merging some adjacent blocks. Consider a case for `n_reps=2`. The two orbital rotation blocks in the middle can be merged into a single orbital rotation block. The `ffsim` package has a pass manager named `ffsim.qiskit.PRE_INIT` to optimize the circuit by merging such adjacent blocks.\n"
"![A diagram showing layers of the LUCJ ansatz.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig9.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"Ansatz LUCJ dengan lapisan berulang bisa dioptimalkan dengan menggabungkan beberapa blok yang berdekatan. Pertimbangkan kasus untuk `n_reps=2`. Dua blok rotasi orbital di tengah bisa digabungkan menjadi satu blok rotasi orbital. Paket `ffsim` memiliki pass manager bernama `ffsim.qiskit.PRE_INIT` untuk mengoptimalkan Circuit dengan menggabungkan blok-blok yang berdekatan tersebut.\n"
"![A diagram showing layers of the LUCJ ansatz.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig9.svg)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2. Optimize for target hardware {#2-optimize-for-target-hardware}"
msgstr "2. Optimalkan untuk hardware target {#2-optimize-for-target-hardware}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we fetch a backend of our choice. We will optimize our circuit for "
"the backend, and then execute the optimized circuit on the same backend to "
"generate samples for the subspace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, kita ambil Backend pilihan kita. Kita akan mengoptimalkan Circuit "
"kita untuk Backend tersebut, lalu mengeksekusi Circuit yang telah "
"dioptimalkan pada Backend yang sama untuk menghasilkan sampel untuk "
"subspace.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we recommend the following steps to optimize the ansatz and make it "
"hardware-compatible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya, kita rekomendasikan langkah-langkah berikut untuk "
"mengoptimalkan ansatz dan membuatnya kompatibel dengan hardware.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Select physical qubits (`initial_layout`) from the target hardware that "
"adheres to the zig-zag pattern (two linear chains with ancilla qubit in-"
"between them) described above. Laying out qubits in this pattern leads to an"
" efficient hardware-compatible circuit with less gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih qubit fisik (`initial_layout`) dari hardware target yang mengikuti "
"pola zig-zag (dua rantai linier dengan qubit ancilla di antaranya) yang "
"dijelaskan di atas. Menata qubit dalam pola ini menghasilkan Circuit yang "
"efisien dan kompatibel dengan hardware dengan lebih sedikit Gate.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Generate a staged pass manager using the "
"[`generate_preset_pass_manager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager)"
" function from Qiskit with your choice of `backend` and `initial_layout`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Buat staged pass manager menggunakan fungsi "
"[`generate_preset_pass_manager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager)"
" dari Qiskit dengan pilihan `backend` dan `initial_layout` kamu.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Set the `pre_init` stage of your staged pass manager to "
"`ffsim.qiskit.PRE_INIT`. `ffsim.qiskit.PRE_INIT` includes Qiskit transpiler "
"passes that decompose gates into orbital rotations and then merges the "
"orbital rotations, resulting in fewer gates in the final circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Atur tahap `pre_init` dari staged pass manager kamu ke "
"`ffsim.qiskit.PRE_INIT`. `ffsim.qiskit.PRE_INIT` mencakup pass Transpiler "
"Qiskit yang mengurai Gate menjadi rotasi orbital dan kemudian menggabungkan "
"rotasi orbital, menghasilkan lebih sedikit Gate dalam Circuit akhir.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run the pass manager on your circuit.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan pass manager pada Circuit kamu.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3. Execute on target hardware {#3-execute-on-target-hardware}"
msgstr "3. Eksekusi pada hardware target {#3-execute-on-target-hardware}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After optimizing the circuit for hardware execution, we are ready to run it "
"on the target hardware and collect samples for ground state energy "
"estimation. As we only have one circuit, we will use Qiskit Runtime's [Job "
"execution mode](/guides/execution-modes) and execute our circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah mengoptimalkan Circuit untuk eksekusi hardware, kita siap "
"menjalankannya pada hardware target dan mengumpulkan sampel untuk estimasi "
"energi ground state. Karena kita hanya memiliki satu sirkuit, kita akan "
"menggunakan [mode eksekusi Job](/guides/execution-modes) dari Qiskit Runtime"
" dan mengeksekusi Circuit kita.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "4. Post-process results {#4-post-process-results}"
msgstr "4. Post-process results {#4-post-process-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The post-processing part of the SQD workflow can be summarized using the "
"following diagram.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagian post-processing dari alur kerja SQD bisa diringkas menggunakan "
"diagram berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A flow chart showing how sampled states are used to determine ground state eigenvalues and eigenvectors.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig10.svg)\n"
"Sampling the LUCJ ansatz in the computational basis generates a pool of noisy configurations $\\tilde{\\mathcal{\\chi}}$, which are used in the post-processing routine. It involves a method called (details discussed later) _configuration recovery_ to probabilistically correct configurations with incorrect electron numbers. Configurations only with correct electron numbers $\\tilde{\\mathcal{\\chi}}_{R}$ are then subsampled and distributed into multiple batches based on the frequency of appearance of each unique configuration. Each batch of samples defines a subspace ($\\mathcal{S^{(k)}}$). Next, the molecular Hamiltonian, $H$, is projected onto subspaces:\n"
"$$\n"
"H_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} = P_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} H _{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} \\text{ with } P_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} = \\sum_{x \\in \\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} \\vert x \\rangle \\langle x \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"![A flow chart showing how sampled states are used to determine ground state eigenvalues and eigenvectors.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig10.svg)\n"
"Pengambilan sampel ansatz LUCJ dalam basis komputasi menghasilkan kumpulan konfigurasi yang bising $\\tilde{\\mathcal{\\chi}}$, yang digunakan dalam rutinitas post-processing. Proses ini melibatkan metode yang disebut _configuration recovery_ (dibahas lebih lanjut nanti) untuk secara probabilistik mengoreksi konfigurasi dengan jumlah elektron yang salah. Konfigurasi yang hanya memiliki jumlah elektron yang benar $\\tilde{\\mathcal{\\chi}}_{R}$ kemudian di-subsample dan didistribusikan ke dalam beberapa batch berdasarkan frekuensi kemunculan setiap konfigurasi unik. Setiap batch sampel mendefinisikan sebuah subspace ($\\mathcal{S^{(k)}}$). Selanjutnya, Hamiltonian molekular, $H$, diproyeksikan ke subspace:\n"
"$$\n"
"H_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} = P_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} H _{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} \\text{ with } P_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} = \\sum_{x \\in \\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} \\vert x \\rangle \\langle x \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each projected Hamiltonian $H_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}}$ is then fed into an "
"Eigensolver, where it is diagonalized to compute eigenvalues and "
"eigenvectors to reconstruct an eigenstate. In this lesson, we project and "
"diagonalize the Hamiltonian using the `qiskit-addon-sqd` package which uses "
"the Davidson's method from PySCF for diagonalization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap Hamiltonian yang diproyeksikan $H_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}}$ kemudian "
"dimasukkan ke dalam Eigensolver, di mana ia didiagonalisasi untuk menghitung"
" nilai eigen dan vektor eigen guna merekonstruksi eigenstate. Dalam "
"pelajaran ini, kita memproyeksikan dan mendiagonalisasi Hamiltonian "
"menggunakan paket `qiskit-addon-sqd` yang menggunakan metode Davidson dari "
"PySCF untuk diagonalisasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} \\vert \\psi^{(k)} \\rangle = E^{(k)} \\vert \\psi^{(k)} \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H_{\\mathcal{S}^{(k)}} \\vert \\psi^{(k)} \\rangle = E^{(k)} \\vert \\psi^{(k)} \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We then collect the lowest eigenvalue (energy) from the batches, and also "
"compute average orbital occupancy, $\\text{n}$. The average occupancy "
"information is used in the configuration recovery step to probabilistically "
"correct noise configurations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita kemudian mengumpulkan nilai eigen (energi) terendah dari batch-batch "
"tersebut, dan juga menghitung rata-rata hunian orbital, $\\text{n}$. "
"Informasi hunian rata-rata ini digunakan dalam langkah configuration "
"recovery untuk secara probabilistik mengoreksi konfigurasi yang bising.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we explain the self-consistent configuration recovery loop in detail "
"and show concrete code examples to implement the above-mentioned steps to "
"estimate the ground state energy of $N_2$ Hamiltonian.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya, kita menjelaskan secara rinci loop configuration recovery yang "
"self-consistent dan menunjukkan contoh kode konkret untuk "
"mengimplementasikan langkah-langkah di atas guna memperkirakan energi ground"
" state dari Hamiltonian $N_2$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"4.1 Configuration recovery: overview {#41-configuration-recovery-overview}"
msgstr ""
"4.1 Configuration recovery: gambaran umum {#41-configuration-recovery-"
"overview}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each bit in a bitstring (Slater determinant) represents a spin orbital. The "
"right half of a bitstring represents spin-up orbitals, and the left half "
"represents spin-down orbitals. A `1` means the orbital is occupied by an "
"electron, and a `0` means the orbital is empty. We know the correct number "
"of particles (both up-spin electron and down-spin electron) a priori. "
"Suppose we have a determinant $x$ with $N_x$ electrons (that is, there are "
"$N_x$ numbers of $1$s in the bitstring) in it. The correct number of "
"particles is $N$. If $N_x \\neq N$, then we know that the bitstring is "
"corrupted by noise. The self-consistent configuration routine attempts to "
"correct the bitstring by probabilistically flipping $|N_x - N|$ bits by "
"leveraging average orbital occupancy information. The average orbital "
"occupancy ($n$) tells us how likely an orbital be occupied by an electron. "
"If $N_x < N$, we have fewer electrons and need to flip some $0$s to $1$s and"
" vice versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap bit dalam sebuah bitstring (determinan Slater) mewakili orbital spin."
" Setengah kanan dari sebuah bitstring mewakili orbital spin-up, dan setengah"
" kiri mewakili orbital spin-down. `1` berarti orbital ditempati oleh "
"elektron, dan `0` berarti orbital kosong. Kita mengetahui jumlah partikel "
"yang benar (baik elektron spin-up maupun spin-down) sejak awal. Misalkan "
"kita memiliki determinan $x$ dengan $N_x$ elektron (yaitu, ada $N_x$ jumlah "
"$1$ dalam bitstring) di dalamnya. Jumlah partikel yang benar adalah $N$. "
"Jika $N_x \\neq N$, maka kita tahu bahwa bitstring tersebut rusak oleh "
"noise. Rutinitas konfigurasi self-consistent mencoba mengoreksi bitstring "
"dengan membalik $|N_x - N|$ bit secara probabilistik dengan memanfaatkan "
"informasi hunian orbital rata-rata. Hunian orbital rata-rata ($n$) memberi "
"tahu kita seberapa besar kemungkinan suatu orbital ditempati oleh elektron. "
"Jika $N_x < N$, kita memiliki lebih sedikit elektron dan perlu membalik "
"beberapa $0$ menjadi $1$ dan sebaliknya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The probability of flipping can be $|x[i] - avg\\_occupancy[i]|$ for `i`-th "
"spin orbital. In [\\[2\\]](#references), the authors used a weighted "
"probability of flipping using modified ReLU function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Probabilitas pembalikan bisa berupa $|x[i] - avg\\_occupancy[i]|$ untuk "
"orbital spin ke-`i`. Dalam [\\[2\\]](#references), para penulis menggunakan "
"probabilitas pembalikan berbobot menggunakan fungsi ReLU yang "
"dimodifikasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align}\n"
"    w(y) = \\begin{cases}\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align}\n"
"    w(y) = \\begin{cases}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "    \\delta \\frac{y}{h} & \\text{if }  y \\leq h\\\\ \\nonumber\n"
msgstr "    \\delta \\frac{y}{h} & \\text{if }  y \\leq h\\\\ \\nonumber\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "    \\delta + (1 - \\delta) \\frac{y - h}{1 - h} & \\text{if } y > h\n"
msgstr "    \\delta + (1 - \\delta) \\frac{y - h}{1 - h} & \\text{if } y > h\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here $h$ defines the location of \"corner\" of the ReLU function, and the "
"parameter $\\delta$ defines the value of the ReLU function at the corner. "
"For $\\delta = 0$, $w$ becomes true ReLU function, and for $\\delta >0$, it "
"becomes _modified_ ReLU. In the paper, the authors used $\\delta = 0.01$ and"
" $h =$ number of alpha (or beta) particles/number of alpha (or beta) spin "
"orbitals $= N/M$ (filling factor).\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini $h$ mendefinisikan lokasi \"sudut\" dari fungsi ReLU, dan parameter "
"$\\delta$ mendefinisikan nilai fungsi ReLU di sudut tersebut. Untuk $\\delta"
" = 0$, $w$ menjadi fungsi ReLU sejati, dan untuk $\\delta >0$, ia menjadi "
"ReLU _termodifikasi_. Dalam paper tersebut, para penulis menggunakan "
"$\\delta = 0.01$ dan $h =$ jumlah partikel alpha (atau beta)/jumlah orbital "
"spin alpha (atau beta) $= N/M$ (faktor pengisian).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The average orbital occupancy ($n$) is not known a priori. The first "
"iteration of the ground state estimation starts with configurations with "
"only correct particle numbers in both spin species. After the first "
"iteration, we have an estimate of the ground state, and using the estimate, "
"we can construct the first guess of $n$. This guess of $n$ is used to "
"recover configurations, run the next iteration of ground state estimation, "
"and self-consistently refine the guess of $n$. The process repeats until the"
" a stopping criterion is met.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hunian orbital rata-rata ($n$) tidak diketahui sejak awal. Iterasi pertama "
"dari estimasi ground state dimulai dengan konfigurasi yang hanya memiliki "
"jumlah partikel yang benar di kedua spesies spin. Setelah iterasi pertama, "
"kita memiliki perkiraan ground state, dan menggunakan perkiraan tersebut, "
"kita bisa membuat tebakan pertama dari $n$. Tebakan $n$ ini digunakan untuk "
"memulihkan konfigurasi, menjalankan iterasi berikutnya dari estimasi ground "
"state, dan secara self-consistent menyempurnakan tebakan $n$. Proses ini "
"berulang sampai kriteria penghentian terpenuhi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider the following example for $N = 2$ and $x = |1000\\rangle$ ($N_x = "
"1$). We need to flip one of the 0s to 1 to correct it for particle numbers, "
"and the choices are `1100`, `1010`, and `1001`. Based on the probability of "
"flipping, one of the choices will be selected as _recovered configuration_ "
"(or the bitstring with correct number of particles).\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan contoh berikut untuk $N = 2$ dan $x = |1000\\rangle$ ($N_x = "
"1$). Kita perlu membalik salah satu dari 0 menjadi 1 untuk mengoreksinya "
"sesuai jumlah partikel, dan pilihannya adalah `1100`, `1010`, dan `1001`. "
"Berdasarkan probabilitas pembalikan, salah satu pilihan akan dipilih sebagai"
" _recovered configuration_ (atau bitstring dengan jumlah partikel yang "
"benar).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose in the first iteration we run two batches, and the estimated ground "
"states from them are:\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalkan pada iterasi pertama kita menjalankan dua batch, dan ground state "
"yang diperkirakan dari keduanya adalah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align}\\nonumber\n"
"    \\text{Batch0: } \\vert \\psi \\rangle &= 0.8 \\times \\vert 1001 \\rangle + 0.6 \\times \\vert 0110 \\rangle \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"    \\text{Batch1: } \\vert \\psi \\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\left( \\vert 1001 \\rangle + \\vert 0101 \\rangle + \\vert 0110 \\rangle \\right) \\nonumber\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align}\\nonumber\n"
"    \\text{Batch0: } \\vert \\psi \\rangle &= 0.8 \\times \\vert 1001 \\rangle + 0.6 \\times \\vert 0110 \\rangle \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"    \\text{Batch1: } \\vert \\psi \\rangle &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\left( \\vert 1001 \\rangle + \\vert 0101 \\rangle + \\vert 0110 \\rangle \\right) \\nonumber\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using the computational basis states and their amplitudes, we can compute "
"probability of electron occupancies (in short _occupancies_) per spin-"
"orbital (qubit) (note that probability = |amplitude|$^2$). Below we tabulate"
" qubit-wise occupancies for each bitstring appearing in the estimated ground"
" state and compute total orbital occupancy for a batch. Note that, as per "
"Qiskit ordering convention, the right most bit represents qubit-0 (Q0), and "
"the left most bit represents Q3.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan state basis komputasi dan amplitudonya, kita bisa menghitung "
"probabilitas hunian elektron (singkatnya _occupancies_) per orbital spin "
"(qubit) (perhatikan bahwa probabilitas = |amplitudo|$^2$). Di bawah ini kita"
" tabelkan hunian per qubit untuk setiap bitstring yang muncul dalam ground "
"state yang diperkirakan dan menghitung hunian orbital total untuk sebuah "
"batch. Perhatikan bahwa, sesuai konvensi pengurutan Qiskit, bit paling kanan"
" mewakili qubit-0 (Q0), dan bit paling kiri mewakili Q3.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Occupancy (Batch0):\n"
"|           |    Q3    |    Q2    |    Q1    |    Q0    |\n"
"|:---------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n"
"|    1001   |   0.64   |    0.0   |    0.0   |   0.64   |\n"
"|    0110   |    0.0   |   0.36   |   0.36   |    0.0   |\n"
"| **n** _(Batch0)_ | **0.64** | **0.36** | **0.36** | **0.64** |\n"
msgstr ""
"Hunian (Batch0):\n"
"|           |    Q3    |    Q2    |    Q1    |    Q0    |\n"
"|:---------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n"
"|    1001   |   0.64   |    0.0   |    0.0   |   0.64   |\n"
"|    0110   |    0.0   |   0.36   |   0.36   |    0.0   |\n"
"| **n** _(Batch0)_ | **0.64** | **0.36** | **0.36** | **0.64** |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Occupancy (Batch1)\n"
"|           |    Q3    |    Q2    |    Q1    |    Q0    |\n"
"|:---------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n"
"|    1001   |    0.33   |   0.00   |   0.00   |    0.33   |\n"
"|    0101   |    0.0   |   0.33   |   0.00   |    0.33   |\n"
"|    0110   |    0.0   |   0.33   |   0.33   |    0.00   |\n"
"| **n** _(Batch1)_ | **0.33** | **0.66** | **0.33** | **0.66** |\n"
msgstr ""
"Hunian (Batch1)\n"
"|           |    Q3    |    Q2    |    Q1    |    Q0    |\n"
"|:---------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n"
"|    1001   |    0.33   |   0.00   |   0.00   |    0.33   |\n"
"|    0101   |    0.0   |   0.33   |   0.00   |    0.33   |\n"
"|    0110   |    0.0   |   0.33   |   0.33   |    0.00   |\n"
"| **n** _(Batch1)_ | **0.33** | **0.66** | **0.33** | **0.66** |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Occupancy (average across batches)\n"
"|           |    Q3    |    Q2    |    Q1    |    Q0    |\n"
"|:---------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n"
"| **n** _(Batch0)_ | 0.64 | 0.36 | 0.36 | 0.64 |\n"
"| **n** _(Batch1)_ | 0.33 | 0.66 | 0.33 | 0.66 |\n"
"| **n** _(average)_ | **0.49** | **0.51** | **0.35** | **0.65** |\n"
msgstr ""
"Hunian (rata-rata antar batch)\n"
"|           |    Q3    |    Q2    |    Q1    |    Q0    |\n"
"|:---------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n"
"| **n** _(Batch0)_ | 0.64 | 0.36 | 0.36 | 0.64 |\n"
"| **n** _(Batch1)_ | 0.33 | 0.66 | 0.33 | 0.66 |\n"
"| **n** _(average)_ | **0.49** | **0.51** | **0.35** | **0.65** |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using the average orbital occupancy computed above, we can find the "
"probabilities of flip for different orbitals in the configuration $x = "
"\\vert 1000 \\rangle$. As the orbital represented by Q3 is already occupied "
"and need not to be flipped, we set its p(flip) to $0$. For the remaining "
"orbitals, which are unoccupied, the probability of flip is $\\vert x[i] - "
"\\text{n}[i] \\vert$ each. Along with p(flip), we also compute the "
"probability weight associated with flipping using the modified ReLU function"
" described above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan hunian orbital rata-rata yang dihitung di atas, kita bisa "
"menemukan probabilitas pembalikan untuk orbital-orbital berbeda dalam "
"konfigurasi $x = \\vert 1000 \\rangle$. Karena orbital yang diwakili oleh Q3"
" sudah ditempati dan tidak perlu dibalik, kita set p(flip)-nya menjadi $0$. "
"Untuk orbital lainnya yang kosong, probabilitas pembalikan adalah $\\vert "
"x[i] - \\text{n}[i] \\vert$ masing-masing. Bersama dengan p(flip), kita juga"
" menghitung bobot probabilitas yang terkait dengan pembalikan menggunakan "
"fungsi ReLU termodifikasi yang dijelaskan di atas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Probability of flip ($x = \\vert 1000 \\rangle$, $\\delta = 0.01$, $h = N/M = 2/4 = 0.50$)\n"
"|           |    Q3    |    Q2    |    Q1    |    Q0    |\n"
"|:---------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n"
"| p(flip) ($\\vert x[i] - \\text{n}[i] \\vert$) | 0 | 0.51 | 0.35 | 0.65 |\n"
"| w(p(flip)) | 0 | 0.03 | 0.007 | 0.31 |\n"
msgstr ""
"Probabilitas pembalikan ($x = \\vert 1000 \\rangle$, $\\delta = 0.01$, $h = N/M = 2/4 = 0.50$)\n"
"|           |    Q3    |    Q2    |    Q1    |    Q0    |\n"
"|:---------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n"
"| p(flip) ($\\vert x[i] - \\text{n}[i] \\vert$) | 0 | 0.51 | 0.35 | 0.65 |\n"
"| w(p(flip)) | 0 | 0.03 | 0.007 | 0.31 |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, using weighted probabilities above, we can flip one of the unoccupied Q2, Q1, and Q0 orbitals. Based on the values above, Q0 will be flipped most likely, and a possible recovered configuration can be $\\vert \\text{1001} \\rangle$.\n"
"![A diagram of configuration recovery.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig11.svg)\n"
"The complete self-consistent configuration recovery process can be summarized as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, menggunakan probabilitas berbobot di atas, kita bisa membalik salah satu dari orbital Q2, Q1, dan Q0 yang kosong. Berdasarkan nilai di atas, Q0 paling mungkin dibalik, dan konfigurasi yang mungkin dipulihkan adalah $\\vert \\text{1001} \\rangle$.\n"
"![A diagram of configuration recovery.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/sqd2/sqd2-fig11.svg)\n"
"Proses configuration recovery self-consistent yang lengkap bisa dirangkum sebagai berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**First iteration:** Suppose the bitstrings (configurations or Slater determinants) generated by the quantum computer form a set $\\widetilde{\\chi}$, which includes both configurations with correct ($\\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct}$) and incorrect ($\\widetilde{\\chi}_{incorrect}$) number of particles in each spin sector.\n"
"1. Configurations from ($\\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct}$) are randomly sampled to create batches $(\\mathcal{S}^{(1)}, \\cdots, \\mathcal{S}^{(K)})$ of vectors for subspace projection. The number of batches and samples in each batch are user defined parameters. The larger the number of samples in each batch, the larger the subspace dimension and more computationally demanding the diagonalization becomes. On the other hand, too small number of samples may miss the ground state support vectors and lead to incorrect estimation.\n"
"2. Run the eigenstate solver (that is, projection onto subspace and diagonalization) on the batches and obtain approximate eigenstates. $|\\psi^{(1)}\\rangle, \\cdots, |\\psi^{(K)}\\rangle$.\n"
"3. From the approximate eigenstates construct the first guess for $n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Iterasi pertama:** Misalkan bitstring (konfigurasi atau determinan Slater) yang dihasilkan oleh komputer kuantum membentuk himpunan $\\widetilde{\\chi}$, yang mencakup konfigurasi dengan jumlah partikel yang benar ($\\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct}$) maupun yang salah ($\\widetilde{\\chi}_{incorrect}$) di setiap sektor spin.\n"
"1. Konfigurasi dari ($\\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct}$) di-sample secara acak untuk membuat batch $(\\mathcal{S}^{(1)}, \\cdots, \\mathcal{S}^{(K)})$ vektor untuk proyeksi subspace. Jumlah batch dan sampel dalam setiap batch adalah parameter yang ditentukan pengguna. Semakin besar jumlah sampel dalam setiap batch, semakin besar dimensi subspace dan semakin berat komputasi diagonalisasi yang dibutuhkan. Di sisi lain, jumlah sampel yang terlalu sedikit bisa melewatkan vektor dukungan ground state dan menghasilkan estimasi yang salah.\n"
"2. Jalankan eigenstate solver (yaitu, proyeksi ke subspace dan diagonalisasi) pada batch-batch tersebut dan dapatkan eigenstate perkiraan. $|\\psi^{(1)}\\rangle, \\cdots, |\\psi^{(K)}\\rangle$.\n"
"3. Dari eigenstate perkiraan, buat tebakan pertama untuk $n$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Subsequent iterations:**\n"
"1. Using $n$ correct the configurations with wrong particle number in $\\widetilde{\\chi}_{incorrect}$. Suppose we name them $\\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct\\_new}$. Then, $\\widetilde{\\chi}_{recovered} (\\widetilde{\\chi}_{R}) = \\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct} \\cup \\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct\\_new}$ forms the new set of configurations with correct particle numbers.\n"
"2. $\\widetilde{\\chi}_{R}$ is sampled to create batches $\\mathcal{S}^{(1)}, \\cdots, \\mathcal{S}^{(K)}$.\n"
"3. Eigenstate solver runs with new batches and generates new estimates of ground states $|\\psi^{(1)}\\rangle, \\cdots, |\\psi^{(K)}\\rangle$.\n"
"4. From the approximate eigenstates construct refined guess for $n$.\n"
"5. If the stopping criterion is not met, go back to step `2.1`.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Iterasi berikutnya:**\n"
"1. Menggunakan $n$ untuk mengoreksi konfigurasi dengan jumlah partikel yang salah dalam $\\widetilde{\\chi}_{incorrect}$. Misalkan kita menamakannya $\\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct\\_new}$. Kemudian, $\\widetilde{\\chi}_{recovered} (\\widetilde{\\chi}_{R}) = \\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct} \\cup \\widetilde{\\chi}_{correct\\_new}$ membentuk himpunan konfigurasi baru dengan jumlah partikel yang benar.\n"
"2. $\\widetilde{\\chi}_{R}$ di-sample untuk membuat batch $\\mathcal{S}^{(1)}, \\cdots, \\mathcal{S}^{(K)}$.\n"
"3. Eigenstate solver berjalan dengan batch baru dan menghasilkan estimasi baru dari ground state $|\\psi^{(1)}\\rangle, \\cdots, |\\psi^{(K)}\\rangle$.\n"
"4. Dari eigenstate perkiraan, buat tebakan yang lebih baik untuk $n$.\n"
"5. Jika kriteria penghentian belum terpenuhi, kembali ke langkah `2.1`.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "4.2 Ground state estimation {#42-ground-state-estimation}"
msgstr "4.2 Estimasi ground state {#42-ground-state-estimation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we will transform the counts into a bitstring matrix and probability "
"array for post-processing.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, kita akan mengubah counts menjadi matriks bitstring dan array "
"probabilitas untuk post-processing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each row in the matrix represents one unique bitstring. Since qubits are "
"indexed from the right of a bitstring in Qiskit, column ``0`` represents "
"qubit ``N-1``, and column ``N-1`` represents qubit ``0``, where ``N`` is the"
" number of qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap baris dalam matriks mewakili satu bitstring unik. Karena qubit "
"diindeks dari kanan bitstring di Qiskit, kolom ``0`` mewakili qubit ``N-1``,"
" dan kolom ``N-1`` mewakili qubit ``0``, di mana ``N`` adalah jumlah "
"qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The alpha orbitals are represented in the column index range ``(N, N/2]`` "
"(right half), and the beta orbitals are represented in the column range "
"``(N/2, 0]`` (left half).\n"
msgstr ""
"Orbital alpha diwakili dalam rentang indeks kolom ``(N, N/2]`` (setengah "
"kanan), dan orbital beta diwakili dalam rentang kolom ``(N/2, 0]`` (setengah"
" kiri).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are a few user-controlled options which are important for this "
"technique:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ada beberapa opsi yang dikendalikan pengguna yang penting untuk teknik "
"ini:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"``iterations``: Number of self-consistent configuration recovery "
"iterations\n"
msgstr "``iterations``: Jumlah iterasi configuration recovery self-consistent\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"``n_batches``: Number of batches of configurations used by the different "
"calls to the eigenstate solver\n"
msgstr ""
"``n_batches``: Jumlah batch konfigurasi yang digunakan oleh berbagai "
"panggilan ke eigenstate solver\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"``samples_per_batch``: Number of unique configurations to include in each "
"batch\n"
msgstr ""
"``samples_per_batch``: Jumlah konfigurasi unik yang disertakan dalam setiap "
"batch\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"``max_davidson_cycles``: Maximum number of Davidson cycles run by each "
"eigensolver\n"
msgstr ""
"``max_davidson_cycles``: Jumlah maksimum siklus Davidson yang dijalankan "
"oleh setiap eigensolver\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "4.3 Discussion of results {#43-discussion-of-results}"
msgstr "4.3 Diskusi hasil {#43-discussion-of-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first plot shows that after a few iterations we estimate the ground "
"state energy within ~24 mH (chemical accuracy is typically accepted to be 1 "
"kcal/mol $\\approx$ 1.6 mH). The second plot shows the average occupancy of "
"each spatial orbital after the final iteration. We can see that both the "
"spin-up and spin-down electrons occupy the first five orbitals with high "
"probability in our solutions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Plot pertama menunjukkan bahwa setelah beberapa iterasi kita memperkirakan "
"energi ground state dalam ~24 mH (akurasi kimia biasanya diterima sebesar 1 "
"kcal/mol $\\approx$ 1.6 mH). Plot kedua menunjukkan hunian rata-rata setiap "
"orbital spasial setelah iterasi terakhir. Kita bisa melihat bahwa elektron "
"spin-up maupun spin-down menempati lima orbital pertama dengan probabilitas "
"tinggi dalam solusi kita.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Although the estimated ground state energy is decent, it is not within the "
"chemical accuracy limit ($\\pm \\approx 1.6$ mH). This gap can be attributed"
" to the small subspace dimension we used above for projection and "
"diagonalization. As we used `samples_per_batch=500`, the subspace is spanned"
" by max $500$ vectors, which is missing vectors from ground state support. "
"Increasing the `samples_per_batch` parameter should improve the accuracy at "
"the expense of more classical compute resources and runtime.\n"
msgstr ""
"Meskipun energi ground state yang diperkirakan cukup baik, namun belum dalam"
" batas akurasi kimia ($\\pm \\approx 1.6$ mH). Kesenjangan ini bisa "
"dikaitkan dengan dimensi subspace yang kecil yang kita gunakan di atas untuk"
" proyeksi dan diagonalisasi. Karena kita menggunakan "
"`samples_per_batch=500`, subspace dibentangkan oleh maks $500$ vektor, yang "
"melewatkan vektor dari dukungan ground state. Meningkatkan parameter "
"`samples_per_batch` seharusnya meningkatkan akurasi dengan mengorbankan "
"lebih banyak sumber daya komputasi klasik dan waktu proses.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"diagonalization-algorithms/qda-4-sqd-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/8cd90034-6ef3-41bd-a847-c115cade82f7-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"diagonalization-algorithms/qda-4-sqd-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/8cd90034-6ef3-41bd-a847-c115cade82f7-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Exercise for the reader {#exercise-for-the-reader}"
msgstr "Latihan untuk pembaca {#exercise-for-the-reader}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Progressively increase the `samples_per_batch` parameter (for example, from "
"$1000$ to $10000$ at a step of $1000$; permitted my your computer's memory) "
"and compare the estimated ground state energies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tingkatkan secara bertahap parameter `samples_per_batch` (misalnya, dari "
"$1000$ hingga $10000$ dengan langkah $1000$; sesuai dengan memori "
"komputermu) dan bandingkan energi ground state yang diperkirakan.\n"

